=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play backup/off ----------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Backup screen proposed for slice 3,$
# drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host, each$
# change on the real plan/apply engine. Nothing on this machine$
# changes: every command and file is the fake's, and its record$
# is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: backup/off$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. hardn.yml says$
# enableBackups: false. A change still backs up what its$
# rollback needs (plan §3.16). Each change is planned, reviewed,$
# confirmed y/N and applied on the real engine; then the screen$
# is read again.$
$
# Backup Settings ##############################################$
$
# Backup Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Backup State         Disabled$
  [+] Backup Path          /var/backups/hardn Not created yet$
   -  Rollback backups are still taken$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Backup State         Turn backups on$
   2) Backup Path          Change backup path$
   3) Verify Directory     Check the path, writing nothing$
   4) Backup Runs          None yet$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-4 or q]: 3$
$
  Only root can change /var/backups, where the first backup$
  makes /var/backups/hardn. Nothing was written.$
$
# Backup Settings ##############################################$
$
# Backup Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Backup State         Disabled$
  [+] Backup Path          /var/backups/hardn Not created yet$
   -  Rollback backups are still taken$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Backup State         Turn backups on$
   2) Backup Path          Change backup path$
   3) Verify Directory     Check the path, writing nothing$
   4) Backup Runs          None yet$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-4 or q]: 1$
$
# Turn Backups On ##############################################$
$
# Backup Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Backup State         Enabled$
$
   -  Save the configuration$
      /etc/hardn/hardn.yml$
      @@ -1,4 +1,4 @@$
       # hardn's configuration (web-01.example.net)$
       username: alice$
      -enableBackups: false               # Backup files before$
      | modifying them$
      +enableBackups: true               # Backup files before$
      | modifying them$
       backupPath: "/var/backups/hardn"  # Path to store backups$
$
  Turn backups on? [y/N, 0 or q]: n$
$
# Operation Cancelled$
$
# Backup Settings ##############################################$
$
# Backup Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Backup State         Disabled$
  [+] Backup Path          /var/backups/hardn Not created yet$
   -  Rollback backups are still taken$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Backup State         Turn backups on$
   2) Backup Path          Change backup path$
   3) Verify Directory     Check the path, writing nothing$
   4) Backup Runs          None yet$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-4 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
